  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://davidkoepsell.com/cfr404#ContinuingDisabilityReview">
    <rdfs:label>continuing disability review</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Periodic review of whether an existing disability continues.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://davidkoepsell.com/cfr404#RemedyProcess"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
      <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="N13b8b8e4cdaa4ebba0dbe7663783b7b0">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://davidkoepsell.com/cfr404#repairPathFor"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://davidkoepsell.com/cfr404#InitialDetermination"/>
      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
    <rdfs:subClassOf>
      <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="N1ce08a3969f1465384f6e26e6204e254">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://davidkoepsell.com/cfr404#appliesCriteria"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://davidkoepsell.com/cfr404#MedicalImprovementReviewStandard"/>
      </owl:Restriction>
    </rdfs:subClassOf>
    <cfr:chainLocus>L7</cfr:chainLocus>
    <cfr:sourceSection>404.1589</cfr:sourceSection>
    <cfr:chunkId>404.1589</cfr:chunkId>
    <cfr:sourceQuote>impairment(s) from time to time to determine if you are still eligible for disability cash benefits. We call this evaluation a continuing disability review. We may begin a continuing disability review for any number of reasons including your</cfr:sourceQuote>
    <cfr:extractionConfidence>high</cfr:extractionConfidence>
    <cfr:approved rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</cfr:approved>
    <cfr:reviewNote>hand-authored chain scaffold; anchored on 'review' in 404.1589</cfr:reviewNote>
    <skos:editorialNote>Phase 4 scaffold term</skos:editorialNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://davidkoepsell.com/cfr404#MedicalVocationalGuideline">
    <rdfs:label>medical-vocational guideline</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>The grid rules directing a conclusion from age, education and work experience.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://davidkoepsell.com/cfr404#InstitutionalCriterion"/>
    <cfr:chainLocus>L2</cfr:chainLocus>
    <cfr:sourceSection>App2-all</cfr:sourceSection>
    <cfr:chunkId>App2-all</cfr:chunkId>
    <cfr:sourceQuote>Sec. 200.00 Introduction. 201.00 Maximum sustained work capability limited to sedentary work as a result of severe medically determinable impairment(s). 202.00 Maximum sustained work capability limited to light work</cfr:sourceQuote>
    <cfr:extractionConfidence>high</cfr:extractionConfidence>
    <cfr:approved rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</cfr:approved>
    <cfr:reviewNote>hand-authored chain scaffold; anchored on 'sustained work capability' in App2-all</cfr:reviewNote>
    <skos:editorialNote>Phase 4 scaffold term</skos:editorialNote>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://davidkoepsell.com/cfr404#DurationRequirement">
    <rdfs:label>duration requirement</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>The 12-month continuous-period condition. Grounded here as a generically dependent continuant, which overrides the baseline's grounding of the same term as an Impairment and a disposition. The baseline reading is wrong on the text: 404.1509 states a condition a claim must satisfy, not a capacity a claimant bears, and BFO makes specifically and generically dependent continuants disjoint, so the two groundings cannot both stand.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://davidkoepsell.com/cfr404#InstitutionalCriterion"/>
    <cfr:chainLocus>L2</cfr:chainLocus>
    <cfr:sourceSection>404.1509</cfr:sourceSection>
    <cfr:chunkId>404.1509</cfr:chunkId>
    <cfr:sourceQuote>rment is expected to result in death, it must have lasted or must be expected to last for a continuous period of at least 12 months. We call this the duration requirement.</cfr:sourceQuote>
    <cfr:extractionConfidence>high</cfr:extractionConfidence>
    <cfr:approved rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</cfr:approved>
    <cfr:reviewNote>hand-authored chain scaffold; anchored on 'duration requirement' in 404.1509</cfr:reviewNote>
    <skos:editorialNote>Phase 4 scaffold term</skos:editorialNote>
  </owl:Class>
